{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03YD", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-zariski}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7280362e80d6ac9189d46ce9213ecd5b97151d14848528a07d7e42b0f1aaadf5", "source_text": "Zariski topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f81ac673b15da26aa2bd9dcd6191f85bd380d7b9c2257cb55e958cb5f3d3f9e", "unit_id": "tag:03YD:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YD", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-section-Zariski}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ddd6f3b3c1f8ace9da7cfc8dd44ccb36f0578e1c19d0413b1c5ab834dbed0a0b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn\nSpaces, Section <REF_0001>\nwe introduced the notion of a Zariski covering of an algebraic space by\nopen subspaces. Here is the corresponding notion with open subspaces\nreplaced by open immersions.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cd71f8c1a0f0cd2ac69b680f7f04b06d84c9f13d7a6c67c6e6a24ed80d85e719", "unit_id": "tag:03YD:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03YD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f_i$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n|X| = \\bigcup\\nolimits_{i \\in I} |f_i|(|X_i|),\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-zariski-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e76fae56c3226e3151fabee0092a70b466b5acf08f6f31c1ff32db92d85286f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5130f120ae0375233c96187329fd5d75eb47b20fb0bc3eb797a2a00c7a5c297e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Zariski covering of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family of morphisms\n<MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nsuch that each <MATH_0007> is an open immersion\nand such that\n<MATH_0008>\ni.e., the morphisms are jointly surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a07e13d99ac9b8db85b0e6233d1f560eb2bf441880023138de85902bcf584ef5", "unit_id": "tag:041G:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YD", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dcbfc120effe337c93eba0f972658e90d7ffc1abca69694e6f93c3178a726e87", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAlthough Zariski coverings are occasionally useful the corresponding topology\non the category of algebraic spaces is really too coarse, and not particularly\nuseful. Still, it does define a site.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0ee55be217da45e7236e5cc443d138415ddbcbb1fd39149399afdeebdc926205", "unit_id": "tag:03YD:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{X' \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0012": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{X' \\times_X X_i \\to X'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e3d9a30bc295880eafea81ddede5c59549b2394c91422582e284bba1fee4680", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6b4fb87f09cd4f55ed57ccc1aba26f0110462cab06e6a4320404499aefdcc558", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0005>\nis a Zariski covering of <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0007> is a Zariski covering and for each\n<MATH_0008> we have a Zariski covering <MATH_0009>, then\n<MATH_0010> is a Zariski covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0011> is a Zariski covering\nand <MATH_0012> is a morphism of algebraic spaces then\n<MATH_0013> is a Zariski covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e87b9c49b0dac6767c4f8aa03044c6a80d5fb0f6a4998cde629b76f71521ca87", "unit_id": "tag:041H:statement"}
